<BR><BR>
Here you can download alternative skins for your timer, which have been submitted by other users.<BR>Unzip and save the graphics file in your UI mod folder using the corresponding file name (should replace existing default file):<BR><BR>
<TABLE BORDER=1 CELLSPACING=0 CELLPADDING=2 BORDERCOLOR=#CCCCCC>
<TR><TD CLASS=note><B>Window</B></TD><TD CLASS=note><B>Graphics File Name</B></TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Actions Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Actions_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Bug Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>BugReport_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Compass Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Compass_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Feedback Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Feedback_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Friends Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Friends_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Gems Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>GemsGame_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Group Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Group_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Help Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Help_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Notes Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>PlayerNotes_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Pet Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>PetInfo_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Player Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Player_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=note>Target Window</TD><TD CLASS=note>Target_Timer.tga</TD></TR>
</TABLE>
<BR>
Note: in order to use these graphics files, you must first <A HREF="customize.asp">generate your custom timer configuration</A> using the configuration tool.<BR><BR>
To submit your own timer skin, send an email to Arista with the following information:<BR>
<LI>Name of skin</LI>
<LI>Your name (as you want it to appear in listing)</LI>
<LI>Your email address (so I can contact you if needed)</LI>
<LI>Whether or not the listing should provide a link to your email</LI>
<LI>Version of the timer the skin is designed for (full, compact, or both)</LI>
<LI>Recommended RGB values for the text color</LI>
<LI>ZIP file containing graphics file and sample screenshot</LI>
<BR><BR>
The skin you submit must be compatible with the XML file that is generated by the configuration tool. The easiest way to create a skin is to start with the <A HREF="download.asp?file=skins/default.zip">default graphics file</A>, then modify its various elements.<BR><BR>

